# E §3.1 step 1 (tally 2.1.7 B4, issue #105; P17): a member that is itself a joint model pins its own members
# first, so its member with no file is LOAD-PIN, before any name its text reads is checked, in run and reprint
# alike. 2.1.6's refcore refused LOAD-NAME unknown id b.zone. (T's M0 format member_nested_absent.)
=== options reprint
=== j.tally
model j
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use m = "m/m.tally" sha256 "4bcae9a9d95227c06160e1a8e17b09280223ee80d52311bde4aa7761f6a108c3"
  note "T, pre-M1 (#97, chunk 4; G3 review, 5815c57, #105, P17): its member m pins b, which has no file"

input y: num

source s "s"
=== m/m.tally
model mm
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use b = "../b/b.tally" sha256 "be4463915516bf956ac4de46e79b2e45f6faa87a9e9fe00817215bc75b232c77"

source s "s"

input w[k in b.zone]: num
=== expect
refused: member m: LOAD-PIN ../b/b.tally doesn't match its sha256 in use b (no such file)
